Description: the lines mc itself sends to a subshell of tcsh (its init, the cd that follows the panels, the commands of the user menu) stay out of the history of tcsh, in memory and in ~/.history; what the user types stays
Origin: azsupport/ports (aZ, 12.11.2026), after the tickets of upstream
 https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/issues/2104 and https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/issues/3063 (bash and zsh skip mc's commands by their
 leading space, ignorespace; tcsh has nothing like it)
Why: Up in Ctrl-O and "history" showed a cd "`printf '%b' '\0057...'`" for each
 directory a panel had been in and the init line of mc with its precmd alias, and
 savehist kept them in ~/.history. Now:
 - the cd: mc writes it into mc.cmd.<pid> of its temporary directory and sends a key
   that its init binds with bindkey -c to "source" that file (tcsh records no command
   of a key binding), then an empty line (not recorded either) for precmd and a new
   prompt; when the file cannot be written, the cd is typed as before;
 - the init line ends with "history -c; history -L": the list tcsh loaded at its
   start ($histfile or ~/.history) again, without that line. The reloaded events get
   new numbers (after those of the first load and of the init line: %h and !N are
   higher than without mc); about 60 ms for 10000 events, once per start of mc;
 - a command mc runs by itself (EXECUTE_HIDE: the user menu, "/bin/sh /tmp/.../mcusr...")
   does not go through the subshell of tcsh: it runs through the shell as in mc without
   a subshell (as the user menu without its prompt already does).
 The commands the user types, in Ctrl-O or at the command line of mc, are typed into
 tcsh as before and stay. mc keeps the directories itself: the "Dir Hist" sections of
 ~/.local/share/mc/history (Alt-Shift-H, Alt-Y, Alt-U). The init also sets edit (the
 key needs the line editor of tcsh). noclobber: precmd keeps ">>" to its FIFO, and mc
 writes the file itself.

